  <p class="muted" style="margin:0.8rem 0 0;font-size:0.8rem">Rule of thumb: nginx is the main thing facing the tailnet and container ports bind to 127.0.0.1. UFW denies other interfaces by default but trusts the whole tailnet, so the loopback binding (not the firewall) is what keeps a container off the tailnet. Two exceptions are visible above: Home Assistant runs on the host network (needed for device discovery), the Arcana dev nodes also bind the tailnet IP directly, and <span class="mono">tailscale serve</span> publishes Arcana on :8443 with a Tailscale-issued Let's Encrypt cert, because mobile browsers only accept web push from a trusted origin (nginx :443 and :4100 use the self-managed cert).</p>
