  <rect class="node k-ext" x="1090" y="340" width="200" height="70" rx="8"/>
  <text class="t" x="1106" y="362">GitHub</text><text class="s" x="1106" y="380">eslick/arcana2 (private)</text><text class="m" x="1106" y="397">push · pull · PRs</text>
  <path class="edge" d="M455 412V540H1190V410" marker-end="url(#a-dev)"/>
  <text class="m tc" x="800" y="534">git push / pull</text>
</svg>
  </div>
  <div class="legend">
    <span><i style="border-color:var(--c-gpu)"></i>Claude Code</span>
    <span><i style="border-color:var(--c-app)"></i>Arcana nodes</span>
    <span><i style="border-color:var(--c-net)"></i>MCP endpoints</span>
    <span><i style="border-color:var(--c-data)"></i>source / data</span>
    <span><i style="border-color:var(--c-ts)"></i>tailnet clients</span>
  </div>
  <ol class="steps" style="margin-top:0.9rem">
    <li><strong>Edit.</strong> Claude Code runs on speedracer (<code>arcana</code> wrapper, over ssh from the laptop) and edits <span class="mono">~/projects/arcana2</span>. The same directory is bind-mounted at <span class="mono">/workspace</span> in both containers.</li>
    <li><strong>Hot reload.</strong> The primary's <span class="mono">dev-watch.sh</span> recompiles on save and tells the follower to load the new modules. Dependency or compile-time config changes need <code>make dev.down dev.up</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Inspect and drive over MCP.</strong> <span class="mono">.mcp.json</span> points at <span class="mono">127.0.0.1:4100</span> for sessions on the server. Tidewave gives eval, docs, logs and SQL; DevMCP gives typed registry, journal, model and lifecycle tools, and every mutating call is audited in journal stream <span class="mono">dev_mcp:audit</span>.</li>
    <li><strong>Check.</strong> Tests and provers run in a container (<code>docker exec arcana-dev make check</code>), never in the live node.</li>
    <li><strong>Remote Claude Code.</strong> A client on another machine sets <code>ARCANA_MCP_HOST</code> to the tailnet IP to use the same two MCP endpoints, and syncs source through GitHub.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="callout">The MCP endpoints have no authentication. The boundary is the <span class="mono">ARCANA_ADMIN</span> gate plus the network bind: loopback and the tailnet IP only, never all interfaces. Details and the system architecture are on the <a href="/arcana.html">Arcana 2 page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

